    "not_offered_as_unrestricted_elective": true,
    "description": "Building upon earlier courses (SC2008), this subject aims to bring students into the realm of real inter-networking. The subject consists of two complementary components. On one hand, several application layer protocols are to be explained, along with their requirements on the underlying networks. One the other hand, practical network design and management methodologies will be introduced; they aim at meeting the application requirements. Emphasis is mostly placed on the practical use and construction of networks, with a bias toward multimedia applications. Advanced materials, such as, peer-to-peer networking will also be covered to prepare the students well for the future career in advanced computer networks."
  },
